</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 791)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Grayscale interface.</b> View &#9656; Grayscale Interface (&#8997;&#8984;G) draws every control, panel and accent without color, so nothing competes with the picture. The picture, the marks on it and the palette&#8217;s swatches keep their color. The web page has the same switch under its <b>?</b> menu.</li>
<li><b>Web share: a clean picture.</b> The clip name and timecode are no longer burned into the web proxy &#8212; the page&#8217;s header already says both. A switch in the Share to Web sheet burns them in as before, for shares that want it.</li>
<li>The playlist button wears a thin outline in the web page&#8217;s orange, so &#8220;the orange button&#8221; means the same thing on both.</li>
<li>Invite activity: how often each person opened the shot list and the guide now rides the viewing report and the activity CSV.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
